  "notes": "A somewhat formal word for raising or keeping animals. It implies ongoing care and management, and is used more broadly than {飼|か}う, which is the everyday word for keeping a pet. {飼育|しいく}する is preferred in professional, institutional, and scientific contexts such as zoos, farms, and research facilities.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {動物|どうぶつ}を{飼育|しいく}する: to raise animals\n- {家畜|かちく}を{飼育|しいく}する: to raise livestock\n- {飼育|しいく}{環境|かんきょう}: breeding environment\n- {飼育|しいく}{員|いん}: animal caretaker, zookeeper\n- {飼育|しいく}{方法|ほうほう}: rearing method\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {飼|か}う: to keep (a pet) — the everyday, casual word for having a pet at home\n- {養殖|ようしょく}する: to farm; to cultivate — used for aquaculture (fish, shellfish, seaweed)\n- {育|そだ}てる: to raise; to bring up — a general word that applies to children, plants, and animals alike",
